## Cross-file label consistency
- Pathway strings identical across contingency table and invasion_success ('AgriForest',
  'Gardening', 'Unintentional'); invaded_niche uses consistent n.agfo/n.gard/n.unint.
- Schema description quirks: (a) change-indicator columns are proportions, not categories;
  (b) 500m/1000m descriptions erroneously say '50-meter radius'.

## Read-only preview of urban gradient (NOT the final analysis)
- Mean n.total per plot by urban.2009.50m bin: zero 0.46 / (0-25%] 1.30 / (>25%] 2.00.
  n.gard 0.16/0.53/0.65; n.unint 0.27/0.71/1.28; n.agfo ~0.03-0.06 (flat).
- D urban 1956->2009 > 5%: n.total 1.66 vs 0.52 (no change); unintentional share of
  occurrences 0.63 vs 0.58; gardening 0.33 vs 0.36; agfo 0.04 vs 0.05.
- 60 plots lost >20% cropland and gained >5% urban (50 m).

## Structural constraint
- invaded_niche_pathways.csv has NO species identities (only per-plot pathway counts);
  invasion_success_pathways.csv has traits but NO urban exposure; no join key.
  -> 'different types' x urban is testable only at the introduction-pathway level.
